# Build context allowlist via deny-everything-then-include is awkward in
# Dockerfile syntax, so keep the context lean by excluding the obvious bulk.
# The Dockerfile needs CLAUDE.md, docker/entrypoint.sh, and the files listed in
# the "files" allowlist of s1-secops-mcp/package.json, which is now COPY'd from
# source instead of installed from npm.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache

# s1-secops-mcp ships from local source now, so what sits beside it in the
# build context matters. data/ is 17 MB, is absent from the package's "files"
# allowlist, is referenced by no code, and holds data/credentials.json. The
# Dockerfile COPYs path by path and never names it, but exclude it here too:
# two independent barriers, because the cost of this one leaking is a
# credential baked into a published image layer.
s1-secops-mcp/data/

# Build artefacts
s1-secops-skills-plugin/dist/
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Heavy reference / test data not needed inside the image
mgmt-console-api/spec/
**/tests/
tests/
spec/
docs/assets/
assets/

# Editor & OS junk
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log

# Office docs (sometimes dropped in the repo root for one-offs)
*.pptx
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.pdf

# Windsurf workflow files (not needed at runtime)
.windsurf/
